\section{Convenience-call status behavior}{

Omitting \code{status} retains diagnoses and warns for nonzero tree
statuses. Explicit \code{status = TRUE} retains diagnoses and suppresses those
warnings. Explicit \code{FALSE} discards the diagnoses, so the numeric helpers
cannot replace failed-tree quantities with missing values.

\code{no_feasible_log} is
a valid result with no logs and remains zero in the numeric helpers.
}

